4	Date:   Thu Sep 3 18:24:08 2026 +0000
5	
6	    feat(starrocks-cn): return the parquet footer row total with the FILES() schema
7	    
8	    The CN already opens every parquet footer to infer the FILES() schema; it now
9	    sums FileMetaData::num_rows over them and returns the total in a new proto2
10	    field, PGetFileSchemaResult.num_rows = 3 (optional, so a stock FE ignores it
11	    and a stock BE never sets it). Exact-or-absent: a node that samples files must
12	    leave it unset, never send a partial sum. The FE prefers the total over the
13	    bytes / width estimate, which makes the leaf cardinalities exact (lineitem
14	    5,999,989,709 instead of 1,230,652,806) and independent of the dataset copy.
15	    
16	    build.rs gains a second guard naming the missing patch, and CI applies every
17	    patches/*.patch through apply-starrocks-patches.sh instead of the nixl patch
18	    by name. The FE patch is regenerated with the one consumption line and its
19	    test. Zero extra I/O on the schema RPC.
20	    
21	    Tested: cargo test -p sirius-starrocks-cn --no-default-features (157 lib
22	    tests; new file_schema and get_file_schema tests incl. the routed RPC and its
23	    error path), clippy -D warnings, fmt; FE JUnit testFooterRowCountPreferred
24	    (1000 / null / 0 / -5); fe-build.
25	    
26	    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
